          %h2#introduction Introduction
          %p The Poincaŕe conjecture can be re-formulated as a conjecture concerning link diagrams. After recalling some preliminaries, we present this diagrammatic formulation.
          %h2#kirby_equivalence Kirby equivalence
          %p
            The
            %em framed Reidemeister moves
            on a link diagram are depicted
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/framed_reidemeister_moves.pdf", :title => "framed reidemeister moves"} here
          %p
            The
            %em Kirby moves
            on a link diagram are depicted
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/kirby_moves.pdf", :title => "kirby moves"} here
          %p
            A pair of link diagrams are
            %em Kirby equivalent
            if there is a finite sequence of framed Reidemeister moves and Kirby moves taking one to the other.
          %h2#fundamental_theorems_on_3manifolds Fundamental theorems on 3-manifolds
          %p We shall rely on the following fundamental theorems, which allow for a diagrammatic approach to the Poincaré conjecture.
          .un_thm
            %h6#theorem_lickorishwallace Theorem (Lickorish-Wallace)
            %p
              Let
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              be a closed, connected, orientable 3-manifold. There is a link diagram
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              such that
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is isomorphic to the 3-manifold obtained by the integral Dehn surgery on
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              in
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{3}
              with respect to the blackboard framing of
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
          .un_thm
            %h6#theorem_kirby Theorem (Kirby)
            %p
              Let
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{0}
              and
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{1}
              be closed, connected, orientable 3-manifolds. Let
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{0}
              (respectively
              = succeed ")" do
                %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{1}
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{0}
              (respectively
              = succeed ")" do
                %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{1}
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{3}
              with respect to the blackboard framing of
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{0}
              (respectively
              = succeed ")." do
                %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{1}
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{0}
              is isomorphic to
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{1}
              if and only if
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{0}
              and
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{1}
              are Kirby equivalent.
          %h2#fundamental_group_of_a_link_diagram Fundamental group of a link diagram
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            be a link diagram, with some choice of orientation. We denote the free group on the arcs of
            %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(L)
          %p
            We define
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{1}(L)
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(L)
            by the normal subgroup generated by words of the form
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi a
                      %mn 3
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %msubsup
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %msubsup
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_3^{-1} a_2^{-1} a_1^{-1} a_2
            %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            as depicted
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/labelled_crossing.pdf", :title => "labelled crossing"} here
          %h2#longitude_of_the_component_of_a_link_diagram Longitude of the component of a link diagram
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_28.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            be a link diagram, with some choice of orientation. The longitude of a component of
            %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_29.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is defined to be the word
            %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_30.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            which we obtain after carrying out the following procedure.
          %ol
            %li
              Pick any arc of
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_31.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_32.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_33.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
              be the empty word.
            %li
              Walk around
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_34.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_35.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_36.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              belongs to same component of
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_37.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              or a different one, we add
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_38.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              to the end of
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_39.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
              if the configuration of orientations at the crossing is as depicted in the first figure
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/longitude.pdf", :title => "longitude"} here
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_40.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b^{-1}
              to the end of
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_41.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
              if the configuration of orientations at the crossing is as depicted in the second figure
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/longitude.pdf", :title => "longitude"} here
            %li
              Stop when we return to the arc we started with, namely
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_42.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
          %p The following is a consequence of the van Kampen theorem.
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_43.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              be a closed, connected, orientable 3-manifold. Let
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_44.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              be a link diagram such that the 3-manifold obtained by the integral Dehn surgery on
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_45.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              in
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_46.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{3}
              with respect to the blackboard framing of
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_47.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is isomorphic to
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_48.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_49.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{1}(M)
              is isomorphic to the group
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_50.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi l
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi l
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{1}(L) / \langle l_1, \ldots, l_n \rangle
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_51.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi l
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l_1
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_52.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi …
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ldots
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_53.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi l
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l_{n}
              are the longitudes of the components of
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_54.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_55.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi l
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi l
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle l_1, \ldots, l_n \rangle
              is the normal subgroup generated by these.
          %h2#diagrammatic_formulation_of_the_poincar_conjecture Diagrammatic formulation of the Poincaré conjecture
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_56.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            be a closed, connected
            = succeed "-manifold." do
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_57.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            %em Poincaré conjecture
            is that if
            %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_58.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{1}(M)
            is trivial (that is to say, isomorphic to a group with one element), then
            %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_59.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is isomorphic to
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_60.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{3}
          %p
            If
            %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_61.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{1}(M)
            is trivial, then
            %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_62.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is orientable. It thus follows from the Lickorish-Wallace theorem, the Kirby theorem, the preceding proposition, and the fact that integral Dehn surgery on the empty link diagram gives
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_63.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{3}
            %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_64.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            has the property that the group
            %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_65.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi l
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi l
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{1}(L) / \langle l_1, \ldots, l_n \rangle
            is trivial, then
            %math#mathml_c54031bf2d0701ba110819ad112477a6e3bcf3e9_66.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is Kirby equivalent to the empty link diagram.
